// SavegameBunker known-games table.
//
// Hand-curated starter list for the Add Game dialog's autocomplete. Entries were
// written from the game's own documentation, its publisher's support pages, the save-path
// convention its engine is known to use, or PCGamingWiki's per-game save-location rows. Only
// the bare path facts were taken and rewritten onto this table's variables; no prose, layout or
// wiki markup was copied, and the table is not a reproduction of PCGamingWiki's dataset.
//
// Sorted by display name. Keep it that way — the file is read top to bottom by people, and Find
// does its own ranking, so file order carries no meaning beyond being easy to scan.
//
// This table goes stale on its own: a game can change its save location in a future patch, and
// every entry here is an unverifiable claim about a machine other than the one it was written on.
// That is exactly why the dialog always resolves and reports what a picked template actually
// finds before the entry can be saved, and why Browse is always available beside it.
//
// Path variables: %SAVEDGAMES%, %DOCUMENTS%, %APPDATA%, %LOCALAPPDATA%, %USERPROFILE%.
